# Desktop-entry activation attempt — issue #35
Date: 2026-11-06 (local session)
Host/session: CachyOS x86_64, Wayland/Hyprland; installed target under /tmp/bodh-install-review/prefix

Command, run from /tmp:
  XDG_STATE_HOME=/tmp/bodh-ticket32-review XDG_DATA_HOME=/tmp/bodh-install-review/share gtk-launch bodh

Observed:
- `gtk-launch` exited 0.
- `desktop-file-validate /tmp/bodh-install-review/share/applications/bodh.desktop` exited 0.
- Immediately after activation, no installed launcher/native Bodh process was visible in `pgrep`, and no `bodh` window was present in `hyprctl clients`.

Result: inconclusive; this is not counted as a successful desktop-menu launch. No pointer or keyboard input was synthesized. The earlier direct invocation of the installed launcher did open the native app (see `GUI-32-REVISED.log`), but that does not establish desktop-entry activation. The cause of the missing observed window was not determined in this trial.
